      <transcript>ERESY</transcript>
      <definition>[=ersy] adj. and n, Of both sexes, hermaphrodite; of both genders, neuter.</definition>
      <page>323</page>
      <examples>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠡᠷᠠᠰᠥ ᠡᠭᠡᠰᠢᠭ</unicode>
          <transcript>-- egesig</transcript>
          <definition> Neuter vowel (the vowel i ).</definition>
        </example>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠡᠷᠠᠰᠥ ᠺᠦᠢᠰᠦ</unicode>
          <transcript>-- kyisy</transcript>
          <definition> Neuter gender.</definition>
        </example>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠡᠮ᠎ᠡ ᠡᠷᠠᠰᠥ</unicode>
          <transcript>em-e --</transcript>
          <definition> Hermaphrodite with preponderantly female characteristics,</definition>
        </example>
        <example>
          <unicode>ᠡᠷ᠎ᠡ ᠡᠷᠠᠰᠥ</unicode>
          <transcript>er-e --</transcript>
          <definition> Hermaphrodite with preponderantly male characteristics.</definition>
        </example>
      </examples>
